## 23. Recommended Learning and Experimentation Workflow

When applying XGBoost to a real dataset:

1. Understand the problem and define the target.
2. Perform exploratory data analysis (EDA).
3. Inspect missing values, duplicates, outliers, and data types.
4. Establish a sensible baseline.
5. Split the data using an appropriate validation strategy.
6. Train a default or lightly configured XGBoost model.
7. Evaluate using relevant metrics.
8. Diagnose overfitting and underfitting.
9. Tune hyperparameters systematically.
10. Compare with Random Forest and other relevant baselines.
11. Analyze feature importance and prediction errors.
12. Save the model and document the experiment.
13. Test the inference pipeline.
14. Monitor performance after deployment when applicable.

